<section id="cc_hero" class="cc_hero">
    <div class="cc_hero_top">
        <div class="cc_hero_badge">100% client-side &middot; nothing uploaded &middot; no account</div>
        <h1 class="cc_hero_title">Give it a table. Get an instant explorer.</h1>
        <p class="cc_hero_sub">Paste a spreadsheet, a CSV, or a JSON array and crossex reads which columns are
            numeric and which are categorical, then hands you scatter plots, box &amp; violin plots, histograms,
            heatmaps, a correlation matrix, a drag-and-drop pivot table, and a WebGL 3D view &mdash; all driven
            by dropdowns, not code.</p>
        <div class="cc_hero_cta">
            <button type="button" class="cc_hero_btn cc_hero_btn_primary" id="hero_demo_btn">Load a demo dataset</button>
            <button type="button" class="cc_hero_btn cc_hero_btn_secondary" id="hero_paste_btn">Paste your own data</button>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hero_stats">
            <div class="cc_hero_stat"><b>12+</b><span>chart types</span></div>
            <div class="cc_hero_stat"><b>40+</b><span>color palettes</span></div>
            <div class="cc_hero_stat"><b>5,000,000</b><span>rows tested</span></div>
            <div class="cc_hero_stat"><b>3 lines</b><span>to embed</span></div>
            <div class="cc_hero_stat"><b>0</b><span>server round-trips</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cc_hero_steps">
        <div class="cc_hs_step">
            <span class="cc_hs_num">1</span>
            <div>
                <b>Load your data</b>
                <p>Paste CSV, TSV, or JSON below, drag &amp; drop a file, or press <i>Load Demo Data</i> to try it instantly.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hs_arrow">&#8594;</div>
        <div class="cc_hs_step">
            <span class="cc_hs_num">2</span>
            <div>
                <b>Pick columns, not chart types</b>
                <p>Choose X and Y from the dropdowns and the right chart draws itself. Add Color or Facets to split it by category.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hs_arrow">&#8594;</div>
        <div class="cc_hs_step">
            <span class="cc_hs_num">3</span>
            <div>
                <b>Explore &amp; share</b>
                <p>The icon strip on the left adds filters, palettes, summary stats, formula columns, a data table, a 3D view, and a pivot table. Share Link rebuilds your exact view for anyone.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cc_hero_features">
        <div class="cc_hf_card">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><circle cx="6" cy="16" r="2" fill="#830862"/><circle cx="12" cy="9" r="2" fill="#830862"/><circle cx="18" cy="13" r="2" fill="#830862"/><path d="M3 21 V3 M3 21 H21" fill="none" stroke="#999" stroke-width="1.3"/></svg>
            <b>The chart type picks itself</b>
            <p>Map columns to X, Y, color, and facets — crossex reads the data types and switches between
                scatter, box, histogram, heatmap, and more automatically. No chart-type dropdown to fight.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hf_card">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="5" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="4" y="9.5" width="16" height="5" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="4" y="16" width="16" height="5" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
            <b>Built for real data, not toy demos</b>
            <p>Chunked parsing, incremental column typing, and smart sampling keep a 5-million-row dataset
                responsive in the browser — with a banner that always shows exactly what's being rendered.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hf_card">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="10" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M8 11 V7 a4 4 0 0 1 8 0 V11" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
            <b>Private by construction</b>
            <p>There's no server: parsing, charting, and stats all run in your tab. Share Link compresses the
                whole view — settings and, for small inputs, the data itself — into the URL. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hf_card">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><path d="M8 6 L2 12 L8 18 M16 6 L22 12 L16 18" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            <b>Drop it into any page</b>
            <p>The whole widget — Vega engine included — is one script tag and a <code>crossex()</code> call.
                Lock axes and hide the panel for a fixed dashboard, or leave it fully interactive. An R
                package wraps the same widget for RStudio, Shiny, and R Markdown.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hf_card">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="5" fill="#830862" opacity="0.55"/><rect x="3" y="3" width="5" height="18" fill="#830862" opacity="0.55"/><line x1="3" y1="14" x2="21" y2="14" stroke="#830862"/><line x1="14" y1="3" x2="14" y2="21" stroke="#830862"/></svg>
            <b>A pivot table and formula engine, built in</b>
            <p>Drag-and-drop pivoting over the full dataset, plus a formula language for computed columns
                (<code>(x - mean(x)) / sd(x)</code>) that compiles once and runs in chunks on multi-million-row data.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc_hf_card">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><circle cx="7" cy="17" r="3" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="17" cy="7" r="3" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M9.2 14.8 L14.8 9.2" fill="none" stroke="#830862" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
            <b>Every setting is shareable and remembered</b>
            <p>Axes, filters, palettes, and transforms persist to your browser between visits. Name a full
                configuration as a Saved View, or copy a Share Link that rebuilds the exact same chart for
                someone else — with nothing sent to any server.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
